# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Font pipeline outputs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The pipelines in tools/ regenerate these; the finished fonts are committed
# under assets/fonts/. Intermediates are large and reproducible.
tools/iconfont/work/
tools/bodyfont/out/
tools/bodyfont/literata-main/
tools/*/lit.zip
tools/*/package-lock.json

# Local repository backups (e.g. from a history rewrite)
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Licensed fonts (local only — never commit)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pangram Pangram faces are "all rights reserved" and free for personal use
# only. This repository is public and MIT-licensed, so committing them would
# redistribute and sub-license them beyond those terms. Not currently used by
# the app; ignored so they cannot be added by accident.
assets/fonts/PPEditorialNew-*.otf
assets/fonts/PPMori-*.otf
# ITC Garamond Std is a commercial Monotype/ITC retail font, not a personal-use
# freebie, so the same reasoning applies even more strongly.
assets/fonts/ITCGaramondStd-*.ttf
# Suffix Serif is a licensed commercial family, currently the local face for
# the serif body slot (see `LOCAL_SERIF` in src/fonts.rs). Local builds pick it
# up from disk; a fresh clone falls back to the embedded Literata.
assets/fonts/Suffix Serif *.otf
